Oboro's IR virtualizer (llvm/lib/Transforms/Obfuscation/Virtualize.cpp)
reimplements three mechanisms whose design comes from amice.  No Rust source
was copied; the code is an independent C++ implementation operating on LLVM IR
and LLVM bytecode structures.

  * Block-local virtual-register reuse, including the "pin PHIs and values
    used outside their defining block, recycle only same-block temporaries"
    rule.  Derived from crates/amice/src/aotu/vm_virtualize/translator.rs
    (build_reuse_plan, alloc_vreg_or_spill).

  * Opcode aliasing: one semantic may be encoded by several byte values, with
    the value chosen deterministically from the function key and the
    instruction position.  Derived from crates/amice-vm/src/isa.rs
    (opcode alias selection).

  * Compare-and-branch superinstruction, which folds a comparison into the
    branch that consumes it.  Derived from crates/amice-vm/src/lowering.rs
    (fuse_icmp_br_if).  Oboro decides fusion from IR use-def information
    instead of scanning bytecode.

Files carrying derived work state the origin in their header and next to the
relevant code.

No other amice source, profile data, ISA description or runtime asset is
included in this repository.
